<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00290">
	<title>Charging limit</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>EV settings 
					<indexterm>charging limit</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig>
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/N_CT25Q027_E.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="e01320">
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/N_CT25Q028_E.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<p>The target battery charge level can be selected when charged with AC charger or DC charger.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>The charging level can be changed by 10%.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>If the target battery charge level is lower than the high voltage battery charge level, the battery will not be charged.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
</concept>